item.description:
Animations are created using &lt;animation&gt;
An animation can either be a tween, spring, bezier or oscillatorexample of a animation&lt;animation&gt; | ID : "spring_0" | Type : "Spring" | Instance : node_1 | Props : { ["Goal"] : &lt;cframe&gt;([&lt;vec3&gt;([0,0,0]),&lt;vec3&gt;([1,0,0])]), ["Property"] : "Offset", ["Damping"] : 0.5, ["Frequency"] : 1, ["Response"] : -1, ["Time"] : 1 }
&lt;/animation&gt;
this matches how you'd use <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Interfaces/Animation" href="api/interfaces/animation.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Cinnamon.Animation.Animate()</a>Animations on compilation are disabled, so to play them you'd have to set their enabled property true after compilationlocal Import = Cinnamon.Compile(source,reference) Import["spring_0"].Enabled = true
Batch animations allow you to animate multiple objects at the same time<br>
Like how you'd use <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Interfaces/Animation" href="api/interfaces/animation.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Cinnamon.Animation.BatchAnimation()</a>batch animations are created using &lt;batchanimation&gt;&lt;batchanimation&gt; | ID : "batch" | Instances : [node_0,node_1] | Props : { ["EasingStyle"] : "Sine", ["EasingDirection"] : "In" } | GroupData : { ["Goal"] = [&lt;cframe&gt;([0,0,5]),&lt;cframe&gt;([0,5,10])] } | Type : "Tween"
&lt;/batchanimation&gt;
<br>Batch Animations are also disabled on compilation, so to play them you'd have to call <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Objects/Animatables" href="api/objects/animatables.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">BatchAnimation.SetEnabled()</a>local Import = Cinnamon.Compile(source,reference) Import["batch"].SetEnabled(true)
Timelines allow for multiple animations to be grouped togethera new entry is represented as ```| [Duration] -&gt; {}
a map is used to describe the changes made to the animation's properties before doing the next animation
Timeline entries are played from top to bottom, using the attached animation as the first animation played&lt;animation&gt; | ID : "tween_0" | Type : "Tween" | Instance : node_1 | Props : { ["Goal"] : &lt;prop&gt;(layout_0,1), ["Property"] : "Offset", ["EasingDirection"] : "In", ["EasingStyle"] : "Sine", ["Time"] : 5 }
&lt;/animation&gt; &lt;timeline&gt; | ID : "timeline_0" | Animation : tween_0 | [1] -&gt; { ["Goal"] : &lt;cframe&gt;([0,10,5]), ["EasingStyle"] : "Back", ["EasingDirection"] : "InOut" } | [1] -&gt; { ["Goal"] : &lt;cframe&gt;([0,0,0]) } &lt;/timeline&gt;
Timelines attach themselves to the animation, so it plays when the animation plays<br>Previous <a class="internal-link" data-href="Template_file_guide/Layouts" href="template_file_guide/layouts.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Layouts</a>

Cinnamon objects are created using blocksformatted as&lt;block&gt; | Property : value
&lt;/block&gt;
Start and end markers must have the same name&lt;container&gt; and &lt;screencontainer&gt; are used to construct UIcontainers and Screen containers accordingly.
UIContainer example
&lt;container&gt; | ID : "containerID" | Origin : &lt;cframe&gt;([0,0,0]) | UI : &lt;ref&gt;("UI")
&lt;/container&gt; Screen Container Example
&lt;screencontainer&gt; | ID : "ScreenContainer123" | DisplayDistance : 12 | UI : &lt;ref&gt;("UI")
&lt;/screencontainer&gt;
you can also parent a UIContainer to another UIContainer&lt;container&gt; | ID : "container_1" | Origin : &lt;cframe&gt;([0,0,0]) | UI : &lt;ref&gt;("UI")
&lt;/container&gt; &lt;container&gt; | ID : "container_2" | Parent : container_1 | Origin : &lt;cframe&gt;([0,0,0]) | UI : &lt;ref&gt;("UI")
&lt;/container&gt;
Elements are created by using &lt;element&gt; inside either &lt;container&gt; &lt;screencontainer&gt;
example:&lt;container&gt; | ID : "node_0" | Origin : &lt;cframe&gt;([0, 10, 0]) | UI : &lt;ref&gt;("UI") &lt;element&gt; | UI : &lt;ref&gt;("Frame") | ID : "node_1" | Offset : &lt;cframe&gt;([0, 0, 0]) | Face : "Front" | Resolution : &lt;vec2&gt;([200,200]) &lt;/element&gt; &lt;/container&gt;
Previous <a class="internal-link" data-href="Template_file_guide/Values" href="template_file_guide/values.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Values</a><br>
Next <a class="internal-link" data-href="Template_file_guide/Layouts" href="template_file_guide/layouts.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Layouts</a>

Animatable (Base class, not usable)type Animatable&lt;T&gt; = { Goal : T, Type : "Tween" | "Spring" | "Bezier" | "Oscillator", Instance : Instance, Property : string, Enabled : boolean, Speed : number, Destroy : (Animatable&lt;T&gt;), Time : number, Origin : T, }
Tweenstype Tween&lt;T&gt; = Animatable&lt;T&gt; &amp; { EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, Time : number, Origin : T, Type : "Tween"
}
Springstype Spring&lt;T&gt; = Animatable&lt;T&gt; &amp; { k1 : number, k2 : number, k3 : number, Previous : T, Velocity : T, Type : "Spring"
}
Bezierstype Bezier&lt;T&gt; = Tween&lt;T&gt; &amp; { P1 : T, P2 : T, Type : "Bezier"
}
Oscillatorstype Oscillator&lt;T&gt; = Tween&lt;T&gt; &amp; { Type : "Oscillator", Frequency : number, Phase : number, WaveForm : (Time : number,Frequency : number,Phase : number) -&gt; number
}
Batch Animationtype BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt; = {Animatable&lt;T&gt;} &amp; { SetEnabled : (BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt;,Enabled : Boolean) -&gt; nil, SetGoals : (BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt;,Goal : {T}) -&gt; nil,
}
AnimTimeline (internal, not useable)type AnimTimeline = { IndexPointer : number, BaseSpeed : number, InitStates : {[string] : any},
} &amp; {{Time : number} &amp; {[string] : any}}

Methods for creating and managing <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Objects/Animatables.md" href="api/objects/animatables.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">animations</a>.Methods:
Animate -&gt; Animatablefunction Animate&lt;T&gt;( Instance : Instance | UI3D_Object, Props : { Type : : "Tween" | "Spring" | "Bezier" | "Oscillator", Property : string, Goal : T, Time : number, -- tween EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, -- Bezier EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, P1 : T, P2 : T, -- Spring Frequency : number, Damping : number, Response : number, -- Oscillator EasingDirection : string, EasingStyle : string, Frequency : number, WaveForm : WaveForm Phase : number, }
) : Animatable&lt;T&gt; Creates a Animation of your choosing
Properties inputted depend on the type of animation
BatchAnimation -&gt; BatchAnimationfunction BatchAnimation&lt;T&gt;( AnimationType : "Tween" | "Spring" | "Bezier" | "Oscillator", _Instances : {Instance | UI3D_Object}, Props : {Property : string}, GroupData : {Goal : {T},P1 : {T},P2 : {T},Phase : {number}}
) : BatchAnimation Creates batch animation
AttachTimeline -&gt; AnimTimelinefunction AttachTimeline( Animatable : Animatable&lt;T&gt;, Timeline : {{Time : number} &amp; {[string] : any}}
) -&gt; AnimTimeline Attaches a timeline table to a animatable
Time represents duration not timestamps
SetGoal -&gt; nilfunction SetGoal&lt;T&gt;(Animated : Animatable&lt;T&gt;,Goal : T) : nil Sets the goal of a single animation
Reset -&gt; nilfunction Reset&lt;T&gt;(Animated : Animatable&lt;T&gt;) : nil Resets an animation

Members:<a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Interfaces/Animation.md" href="api/interfaces/animation.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Animation</a> - Methods for creating and handling animation<br>
<a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Interfaces/Layout.md" href="api/interfaces/layout.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Layout</a> - Handles layouts and provides template layoutsMethods:GetUI_3D -&gt; UIContainerfunction GetUI_3D(ScreenGui) : UIContainer Clears out and destroys child objects without destroying the container
NewContainer -&gt; UIContainerfunction NewContainer( ScreenGui, Origin : CFrame
) : UIContainer Creates a new UI container
NewScreenContainer -&gt; ScreenContainerfunction NewScreenContainer( ScreenGui, DisplayDistance : number
) : ScreenContainer Creates a new ScreenContainer
Destroy -&gt; nilfunction Destroy( UI3D_Object : {Destroy : (T) -&gt; nil},
) : nil Deletes anything with a internal destroy method
Compile -&gt; {string : UI3D_Object}function Compile(Source : string,Reference : {[string] : any}) generates cinnamon objects using template source code and a table of external references

Handles layouts and provides template layoutsMethods:ApplyLayout -&gt; nilfunction ApplyLayout( Elements : {Element}, Layout : {CFrame}
) : nil Applies the layout to a table of elements
Templates:
Radial - Places elements in a ring formationfunction Radial(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, Distance: number, StartAngle : number, Padding : number, Axis : Vector3 }
)
List - Places elements in straight linefunction List(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, FillDirection : Vector3, UpDirection : Vector3, ItemsUntilWrap : number, Padding : number, }
)
Grid - Places elements on a gridfunction Grid(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, LookDirection : Vector3, RowSize : number, ColumnSize : number, Padding : Vector2 }
)
Quad bezier - Places Elements along a bezier curvefunction QuadBezier(Elements : {Lookup.Element}, Props : { Origin : CFrame, P1 : CFrame, Goal : CFrame, Padding : number }
)
PlaceFromUDim2 - Places Elements according to its UI position, relative to its container originfunction PlaceFromUDim2( Elements : {Lookup.Element}, DisplayDistance
)

Holds <a class="internal-link" data-href="API/Objects/Element.md" href="api/objects/element.html" target="_self" rel="noopener nofollow">Elements</a> and positions them on the screen.Properties:Enabled : Boolean
Enables/Disables child objects
Debug : Boolean
Adds/Removes itself and its child objects from the debug visualiser
DisplayDistance : number
How far the elements are from the screen
Members: Elements : {Element}
The Elements being stored
UI : ScreenGui
The UI that stores your Elements
Methods:Element -&gt; Elementfunction Container:Element(Props : { UI : GuiObject, Offset : CFrame, Resolution : Vector2, Face : Enum.NormalId }
) : Element creates a new element
Clear -&gt; nilfunction Container:Clear() : nil Clears out and destroys child objects without destroying the container
UDim2ToCFrame -&gt; CFramefunction Container:UDim2ToCFrame( Position : UDim2, ViewPortSize : Vector2, DisplayDistance : number
) : CFrame Projects UDim2 to a position relative to the origin
Partsize -&gt; Vector3
function Container:UDim2ToCFrame( Position : UDim2, ViewPortSize : Vector2,
) : CFrame Calculate how large a element should be using position and viewport size
